<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/glossary#secretary-general-of-the-united-nations">Glossary</a> · Term · office</p><h1 class="enc-title">Secretary-General of the United Nations</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1945">1945</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Secretary-General of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-nations">United Nations</a> is the chief administrative officer of the United Nations and head of its Secretariat, appointed by the General Assembly on the recommendation of the Security Council, usually for five-year terms. The office has also become an important diplomatic role in mediating conflicts. Holders have included <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dag-hammarskjold">Dag Hammarskjöld</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sweden">Sweden</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/u-thant">U Thant</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/burma">Burma</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/javier-perez-de-cuellar">Javier Pérez de Cuéllar</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peru">Peru</a>.</p></div>
